LICENCE
=======

Copyright (c) University of Bristol (Bristol Centre for Supercomputing, BriCS).

This repository contains material under more than one licence, following the
approach used by https://github.com/isambard-sc/docs.isambard.ac.uk (see its
CONTRIBUTING.md, "Licences used"). Use the licence that matches the type of
file, as summarised below.

| Licence      | Applies to                                                  |
| ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| CC-BY-SA-4.0 | Skill content derived from docs.isambard.ac.uk (section 1)  |
| MIT          | Code and tooling (section 2)                                |
| CC0-1.0      | Agent instruction files (section 3)                         |
| Proprietary  | The `brics-hpc-ai-code` skill (section 4)                   |

Where a file states its own licence, that statement takes precedence. For
skills, this is the `license` field in the YAML frontmatter of `SKILL.md`.


1. Skill content derived from the documentation: CC BY-SA 4.0
-------------------------------------------------------------

The skills under `site/plugins/isambard/skills/` whose `license` field reads
"CC-BY-SA-4.0" (everything in the skill directory, including `references/`)
contain Markdown content derived from https://docs.isambard.ac.uk/. They are
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
licence:

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode

Attribution: "Markdown/image content derived from https://docs.isambard.ac.uk/,
(c) Bristol Centre for Supercomputing (BriCS)."

If you adapt or redistribute this content you must give appropriate credit,
indicate any changes made, and distribute your contributions under the same
licence.

At the time of writing this applies to: containers, cuda, data-transfer,
getting-support, modules, mpi, nccl, python, slurm, spack.

Example commands and scripts that appear in these skills are taken from
documentation pages; the documentation repository releases its example-script
snippet files under CC0-1.0, but the skill text around them is CC BY-SA 4.0.


2. Code and tooling: MIT
------------------------

The programs and build files that validate, build or publish the skills site
are licensed under the MIT licence:

    https://opensource.org/license/mit

This covers:

  * `.github/workflows/` (workflows and the Python scripts in `scripts/`);
  * `site/index.html` and other files that build the published site.

Plugin and marketplace metadata (`.claude-plugin/`, `site/marketplace.json`,
`site/plugins/isambard/.claude-plugin/`) and `site/CNAME` are configuration,
not code. In the documentation repository, site and tool configuration is
CC0-1.0 or CC-BY-SA-4.0 and is not treated as code, and the same is intended
here; these files are covered by section 3 until a specific licence is recorded.


3. Agent instruction files and configuration: CC0 1.0
-----------------------------------------------------

Developer-tooling helpers for agents (`.github/agents/`), editor settings
(`.vscode/`), and the configuration files named at the end of section 2 are
released under CC0 1.0 Universal, as the equivalent files are in the
documentation repository:

    https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode


4. Policy skill: proprietary
----------------------------

The skill `brics-hpc-ai-code` describes BriCS policy and acceptable-use
requirements. Its `license` field reads "Proprietary. See
https://docs.isambard.ac.uk/policies/ for terms." It is NOT licensed under
CC BY-SA 4.0. No right to copy, modify or redistribute it is granted except as
those terms allow or as BriCS otherwise permits in writing. The published
BriCS policies remain authoritative over this skill.

Note: the policy pages in the documentation repository carry an inline
CC-BY-SA-4.0 header, and only the logos, favicons and HPE PDFs there are all
rights reserved. This section records the licence the skill currently
declares; it has not been reconciled with that header.


5. Adding or changing a skill
-----------------------------

Every skill must declare its licence in its `SKILL.md` frontmatter (checked by
`.github/workflows/scripts/check_skill_frontmatter.py`). When a skill is added
or its licence changes, update the lists in sections 1 and 4.


6. No warranty
--------------

Content is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. Always check the
current documentation at https://docs.isambard.ac.uk/ before relying on it.
